Recent bug reports: 
RPT#COMPRESS-302: {
 "summary": "Retore immutability/thread-safety to ArchiveStreamFactory"
 "description": "[](https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/COMPRESS-180 \"new String(byte[]) conversions use default encoding\") added support for encoding. Unfortunately this was done in a way that broke immutability. Also the factory is no longer thread-safe as the encoding field is not synch/volatile."
}

RPT#COMPRESS-297: {
 "summary": "Cleaning up unclosed ZipFile for archive"
 "description": "If you try to create a ZipFile from a non-existent file, then it throws a FileNotFoundException, which is fine. The problem is that the constructor appears to leave behind objects that the caller cannot close. So, later on when the garbage collector runs, a message is printed to stdout that says \"Cleaning up unclosed ZipFile for archive\"."
}

RPT#COMPRESS-303: {
 "summary": "Restore immutability/thread-safety to CompressorStreamFactory"
 "description": "CompressorStreamFactory was immutable prior to 1.5; r1453945 broke immutability. It's also no longer thread-safe because the field decompressConcatenated is not safely published. It would be possible to make it thread-safe by making the field volatile."
}
